also called the common cuckoo.

03:04.720 --> 03:07.940
Is working the register with 
me really that boring?

03:07.940 --> 03:09.620
Not at all!

03:09.620 --> 03:14.400
Being on the register with you is 
the only reason I work here at all!

03:15.970 --> 03:17.680
Well, I'm honored.

03:17.680 --> 03:20.660
But you shouldn't tease your elders.

03:20.660 --> 03:23.360
Come back in another ten years, young man.

03:23.360 --> 03:24.930
Ten years, huh?

03:25.390 --> 03:30.190
If I wait ten years, you'll have matured 
into a truly attractive older woman.

03:30.540 --> 03:31.850
Uh-huh.

03:31.850 --> 03:34.690
So you're not teasing me, 
you're making fun of me.

03:34.690 --> 03:36.830
But we really have nothing to do right now.

03:38.980 --> 03:41.880
Bookstores everywhere are 
closing one after another.

03:41.880 --> 03:44.700
I guess people just don't need them anymore.

03:47.210 --> 03:49.270
You sound sleepy.

03:49.270 --> 03:51.260
Were you up all night writing?

03:51.260 --> 03:53.250
Well, thank you for asking!

03:53.250 --> 03:57.070
You know how more info on Kisaragi Station 
came up yesterday on that occult forum?

03:57.070 --> 03:58.470
Oh, you mean that thing?

03:58.960 --> 04:03.090
That made-up, toothless urban 
legend that's clearly a lie?

04:03.090 --> 04:06.730
I'm amazed someone your age is still 
entertained by such nonsense—ow.

04:07.090 --> 04:11.480
None of that stopped <i>you</i> from reading it, 
so you're in no position to talk, youngster!

04:11.480 --> 04:12.900
"Youngster"?

04:13.300 --> 04:15.600
Through the occult, we can enjoy 
our fear and hesitation

04:15.600 --> 04:17.660
toward things that are beyond 
human understanding.

04:17.660 --> 04:23.490
It stimulates core needs akin 
to hunger and sexual appetite!

04:24.430 --> 04:27.010
So basically, Sumireko-san...

04:27.010 --> 04:31.360
you spent the night absorbed in something 
that acts on base instincts like porn does?

04:31.360 --> 04:32.250
What?

04:32.610 --> 04:36.300
It sounds to me like you didn't 
understand what I was saying at all.

04:36.300 --> 04:37.760
Well, this is a surprise.

04:37.760 --> 04:39.220
Manager.

04:39.220 --> 04:41.980
I've never heard Adashino-kun speak so much.

04:41.980 --> 04:44.260
Yes, he's been unexpectedly chatty.

04:44.260 --> 04:46.060
Infuriatingly so.

04:46.060 --> 04:46.940
Right?

04:48.550 --> 04:51.960
Hey, you can't just clam up now.

04:51.960 --> 04:53.270
You didn't know?

04:53.270 --> 04:56.910
Adashino-kun only speaks 
with you, Ogawa-san.

04:56.910 --> 04:58.340
Oh, right.

05:00.030 --> 05:02.050
A present for you.

05:02.050 --> 05:03.530
What is it?

05:03.530 --> 05:05.620
A book that was reverse-shoplifted.

05:05.620 --> 05:07.040
Reverse-shoplifted?

05:07.360 --> 05:09.110
You haven't heard of it?

05:09.110 --> 05:11.290
The name says it all. 
It's the opposite of shoplifting.

05:11.600 --> 05:15.540
It's when, rather than stealing our stock, 
someone leaves extra behind.

05:15.540 --> 05:18.580
Sounds like a disgruntled customer 
with an axe to grind.

05:18.580 --> 05:21.460
Well, we could just leave it at that, but...

05:21.460 --> 05:25.260
Ogawa-san, it's your birthday, isn't it?

05:25.260 --> 05:27.560
Well, yes...

05:28.560 --> 05:30.100
<b>Newcomer's Award Presentation Ceremony</b>

05:32.240 --> 05:33.560
Sumireko-san.

05:34.150 --> 05:37.160
How is that new novel you 
mentioned before going?

05:37.750 --> 05:40.220
I haven't been able to write lately.

05:40.220 --> 05:41.780
I need to pull myself together.

05:41.780 --> 05:44.820
And you're still treating me 
like we're not friends.

05:44.820 --> 05:48.850
If you'd told me it was your birthday, 
I'd have gotten you a present.

05:48.850 --> 05:50.830
Then here's your chance.

05:51.410 --> 05:52.330
<b>Ogawa</b>

05:52.920 --> 05:56.460
Your consideration in leaving 
your depressed senpai alone

05:56.460 --> 05:58.340
would be the best present I could hope for.

05:59.970 --> 06:02.670
I couldn't possibly just leave you alone.

06:02.670 --> 06:06.850
Despite how it may seem, I am a fan 
of the author Ogawa Sumireko.

06:08.850 --> 06:10.600
Yeah, just keep talking.

06:12.730 --> 06:16.480
<b>Midori Bookstore</b>

06:13.120 --> 06:16.480
<i>I'll make a note of it here so I don't forget.</i>

06:16.880 --> 06:19.480
<i>This is me, Ogawa Sumireko...</i>

06:19.930 --> 06:22.990
<i>and my friend who's never at a loss 
for something to say, Adashino Ren.</i>

06:23.460 --> 06:26.740
<i>What follows is but a humble account 
of our friendship and parting.</i>

06:27.240 --> 06:28.840
Well, I'll see you tomorrow.

06:28.840 --> 06:30.240
Yeah. Goodnight.

07:07.650 --> 07:09.620
<i>Congratulations!</i>

07:18.940 --> 07:22.300
Happy 28th birthday, me.

07:19.210 --> 07:22.300
<b>Happy 28th Birthday, Me</b>

07:25.730 --> 07:28.300
<i>Back then, I could write anything.</i>

07:29.880 --> 07:32.850
<i>When I was fifteen, 
I received a newcomer's award.</i>

07:32.180 --> 07:34.180
<b>Simply Walk Alone, Like a Rhino's Horn</b>

07:34.180 --> 07:38.190
<b>Simply Walk Alone, Like a Rhino's Horn</b>

07:35.990 --> 07:40.050
<i>But past the age of twenty, someone 
like that is just an ordinary person.</i>

07:36.640 --> 07:38.190
<b>Ogawa Sumireko</b>

07:40.790 --> 07:44.430
<i>That's me, I guess. An ordinary person.</i>

07:45.300 --> 07:47.230
<i>I wish I could go back to how I was then.</i>

07:52.080 --> 07:54.080
Oh, for crying out loud.

08:00.320 --> 08:02.350
I can't even read the title.

08:06.090 --> 08:08.740
It seems like Japanese, 
but it's slightly different.

08:09.090 --> 08:10.980
But there's hiragana here.

08:10.980 --> 08:12.720
